          "Ed5aba638083f7fca-B0077",
          "Ed5aba638083f7fca-B0079",
          "Ed5aba638083f7fca-B0080",
          "Ed5aba638083f7fca-B0081"
        ],
        "limitations": "The authors acknowledge that CPA depends on the last subject token serving as a stable causal hub, which weakens on interrogative prompts, as shown by lower efficacy and generalization on zsRE. They also note the sequential two-phase optimization adds roughly 5 seconds of latency per edit, and they identify sequential batch editing in lifelong learning as an open direction.",
        "method_assessment": "The method is clearly specified. CPA is a two-phase optimization framework: Phase 1 optimizes a relation anchor h_r by maximizing log P(o* | h_r) with a KL regularizer, and Phase 2 optimizes the subject injection vector v_s to reconstruct the frozen anchor via a Frobenius-norm loss. The paper provides the theoretical decomposition, implementation equations, layer selection strategy, hyperparameters, and stopping criteria, making the approach reproducible in principle.",
        "quality_rationale": "The paper makes a substantive scoped contribution by diagnosing a shortcut-learning pathology in locate-then-edit knowledge editing and proposing a principled two-phase causal path alignment remedy. The method is adequately described, and the evaluation is meaningful and multi-faceted, including benchmark comparisons, ablations, mechanistic validation, generalization tests, sensitivity analysis, and explicit reporting of a failure mode on zsRE. Claims are generally justified by the reported evidence, and limitations are compatible with the contribution scope.",
        "scoped_contribution": "The paper identifies Subject-Dominant Shortcut as a root cause of Subject-Dominant Memory Interference in in-parameter knowledge editing and introduces Causal Path Alignment (CPA), a two-phase optimization framework that anchors parameter updates to relation-aware intermediate states. The contribution is scoped to single-edit declarative factual knowledge editing in locate-then-edit pipelines, with demonstrated portability to ROME, MEMIT, and AlphaEdit.",
        "source_content_hash": "bbd08d38d12ccd97766992bfbb6e3cd58adb1e540d9750aec247549a4db3a7e5"
      },
